::scene TITLE

ROOM studio_stage

EVENT FADE_IN

TITLE everstock_logo

♪ A relentlessly cheerful jingle, played on an instrument that is not quite a xylophone. ♪

::scene COMMERCIAL

CAM 1 WIDE

SHOT
A warehouse aisle that goes past the vanishing point. Shrink-wrapped pallets stacked four high: cooking oil, cooking oil, cooking oil, machine pistols, cooking oil.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
Everstock. Forty years of not asking what you want it for.

CAM 2 TRACKING pallet_aisle

SHOT
The camera trundles past a pallet of Rattlecans, spray-painted six different colours because the paint was also on offer.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
The Everstock Rattlecan machine pistol. Sold by the pallet, beside the drums, under the same warranty as the drums.

NARRATOR:
Does it jam? Our manual describes this as a cadence feature.

OVERLAY
EVERSTOCK BULK SUPPLY

MINIMUM ORDER: TWELVE

NO, WE WILL NOT SPLIT A PALLET
OVERLAY_END

SHOT
A shopper stands holding a single Rattlecan, looking around for someone to ask. There is nobody. There has never been anybody.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
Everstock. It empties a magazine before it decides to agree.

3s

NARRATOR:
So does the cooking oil, in fairness.

EVENT FADE_OUT

END
